  "kind": "stage",
  "description": "A stage play for reading and rehearsal: 12-point type, lines set as verse with the speaker above each speech in small capitals and the directions in italics, each act on a new page, the scenes within it headed; wide margins for notes.",
  "source": {
    "name": "Standard manuscript format, as the article of that name has it, with the speeches as verse: the common shape of the script formats of theatres and writers' guilds",
    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_manuscript_format",
    "checked": "2026-10-01",
    "confidence": "low",
    "notes": "Theatres and guilds publish formats that agree on the broad shape (the speaker above the speech, directions set apart in italics, acts and scenes headed) and differ in the details; none is reproduced here. Write each speech as verse, with the speaker as a speaker line and stage directions as direction lines; prose speeches are verse of one long line each. Acts are headings of the first level, scenes of the second."
  },
